<article class="env-definition" id="35E766">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/35E766">Definition <span data-tag="35E766">2.3.4.15</span>.</a>truncated!space Let $k \geq -1$ be an integer. A Kan complex $X$ is <em>$k$-truncated</em> if, for every $i > k$ and every point $x \in X$, we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \pi _{i}(X,x) \simeq \ast . \]
</div>
  <p> By convention, we will also say that $X$ is <em>$(-2)$-truncated</em> if $X$ is contractible. </p>
</article>